<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<chapter xml:id="ch-linear-systems" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Systems of Linear Equations</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
      A system of linear equations may have exactly one solution, no solutions at all, or
      infinitely many. Which of these occurs, and how to describe the solutions when there
      are infinitely many, is the subject of this chapter. The tool that settles every
      case is a single mechanical procedure <mdash /> the row reduction algorithm <mdash />
      applied to a rectangular array of numbers called the augmented matrix.
    </p>
  </introduction>

  <xi:include href="linear-systems/sec-systems-of-linear-equations.ptx" />
